This is Meltie's Clicker Picker.

The Browned Butter Babe (BBB) mascot is Braunhilda von Meltington. We call her
Meltie for short. She is a melting pat of butter, and she is probably the most
adorable thing you have seen all day.

Last year, Meltie ran off with BBB's R&D budget and created this clicker
picker in order to help customers pick among the delicious treats sold by BBB.

The clicker picker combines the best in modern technical buzzwords, including
quantum computing, blockchain, and artificial inteligence. Meltie designed a
sophisticated large sugar model (called Sucrose) to look deeply into your soul
and provide a customized and personalized recommendation for a sweet treat.
When training the model, the waste heat is used the bake the BBB treats.

Because of Meltie's tireless work, we are no longer a typical run-of-the-mill
bakery...we are a tech company. :P

# Tech used

* Adafruit Circuit Playground Express (CPE)
* neopixel led strip
* solder
* tears of a site reliability engineer

# Use of the code

The main code is located in melties_clicker_picker.ino.

You must define the following constants near the top of the code:
* NEO_PIXEL_PIN - the number of the neopixel gpio pin
* PIXEL_COUNT - the number of pixels on your neopixel strip
* NUM_CHOICES - the number of choices that are available

In general, Meltie modifies the NUM_CHOICES constant and recompiles and uploads
the resulting firmware to a CPE via the Arduino IDE.

# Arduino IDE requirements

This software requires the installation of board support for the CPE. This is
available via the board manager in the Arduino IDE. The package is named
"Arduino SAMD Boards".

The following Arduino libraries need to be installed from the Arduino IDE
library manager also:
* Adafruit Circuit Playground
* Adafruit NeoPixel
* React_Generic

